  "rationale": "The scenario partition uses two dimensions (gasoline price trajectory and core CPI) but strictly links them with 'AND' clauses, creating significant gaps. For example, a case where gasoline prices remain elevated but core CPI is weak (0.0%) matches no scenario. Similarly, if core CPI exceeds 0.3%, it falls outside all scenarios. The boundary at exactly 0.2% core CPI overlaps between 'high_gas_sticky_core' and 'moderate_gas_soft_core' depending on the gasoline outcome. Because of these gaps and overlaps, the partition is invalid. Regarding the probability, 79.5% underestimates the impact of early September gasoline price surges combined with a very favorable September seasonal adjustment for gasoline (historically adding ~2% to the NSA change). This virtually guarantees a strong positive energy contribution, making a headline print >0.2% highly probable.",
